# Cloudflare Pages, by default, caches static assets aggressively at the
# edge (nav.css was observed being served with "public, max-age=14400" —
# 4 hours — with no _headers file setting that explicitly). During active
# development, that means a pushed fix can take up to 4 hours to actually
# reach a visitor's browser, which reads as "the fix didn't work" even
# though the deployed file is correct. This shortens it to 5 minutes for
# the files that change most often (the shared nav/banner and the pages
# actively being iterated on) so pushes show up close to immediately.
#
# Once the site design stabilizes, these can be safely raised again (or
# removed, to fall back to Cloudflare's longer defaults) for better
# caching performance.

/nav.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate

/nav.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate

/nav-partial.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate

/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate
